#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069298 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068720 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5df52cb5-75b1-58d9-8535-07c1bb87be34" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Length of a Segment"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cb02b8c2-6052-5344-bd63-76a305de6ad4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066959} {:answer/id #uuid "1ed8914b-2c33-5cd7-b590-24eb9cc510af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066960} {:answer/id #uuid "31364172-3f62-5555-8a11-471d0ccd8975" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066961} {:answer/id #uuid "3642a4f3-446d-56be-adcc-079047c7073c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066962} {:answer/id #uuid "63cd08d2-1c61-50aa-9bc5-af6124683d74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066963}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb02b8c2-6052-5344-bd63-76a305de6ad4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066959} :answer-field/id #uuid "696fc38f-3bfd-5221-8c8a-f75c6758af31" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066958}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6c3f5ab6-4dad-5406-88ac-0eb7720cb5c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-3701" :question/problem "![](images/9a/9a2fe4ad55bbc2853ce6f0507780292ae01616df0a2595ff108e674eb91b2557.png)\n\nWhat is the length of $\\overset{―}{AB}?$" :question/worked-solution "From the figure, we note that the points $A$ and $B$ have coordinates ${{(4,2)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{1}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{1})}$ and ${{(8,3)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{2}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{2})},$ respectively. \n\nTo find the distance $AB,$ we can use the distance formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\sqrt{({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})^{2}+({y}_{2}-{y}_{1})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(8-4)^{2}+(3-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{17}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069299 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068721 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bdded031-fd95-5a7f-92d4-c0d6713ba64d" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Distance Between Two Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "84f9576b-3c49-58d5-b0cf-3be799853487" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{27}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066965} {:answer/id #uuid "ed906fd7-c616-5b92-98ac-8e345f436178" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066966} {:answer/id #uuid "fbe93849-2cb6-5c4b-92d9-24a564948aee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066967} {:answer/id #uuid "4adb34e7-c885-5b78-aaa4-9bed521b95d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066968} {:answer/id #uuid "6dfd6889-eff1-5096-802f-6ddf0679ad20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066969}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4adb34e7-c885-5b78-aaa4-9bed521b95d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066968} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5f61f9a-7bb2-5f98-b5a6-d1d9290326b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066964}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0e35e59e-36bb-5c2e-8441-bc45ce18079d" :question/math-academy-id "q-3702" :question/problem "What is the distance between the points $(-9,2)$ and $(-12,-4)?$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we have ${{(-9,2)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{1}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{1})}$ and ${{(-12,-4)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{2}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{2})}.$\nSo, the distance $d$ can be calculated using the distance formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\sqrt{({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})^{2}+({y}_{2}-{y}_{1})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-12-(-9))^{2}+(-4-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+(-6)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+36} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{45} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535030 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068720 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5df52cb5-75b1-58d9-8535-07c1bb87be34" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Length of a Segment"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0eec1ef8-9fdc-5230-9417-7755a8d0b87e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534296} {:answer/id #uuid "0f8e6dec-43af-5f80-ab1e-3eef631db8bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534300} {:answer/id #uuid "43e972e7-cf56-5b6c-b604-0698d249e7cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534393} {:answer/id #uuid "9dda4d19-a039-5a94-a7cf-7a1838c89803" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534617} {:answer/id #uuid "e6e5abdb-b91e-58f8-a040-8654f0c602a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534774}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0eec1ef8-9fdc-5230-9417-7755a8d0b87e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534296} :answer-field/id #uuid "50de03fc-f361-5d04-9b42-75d709112b35" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534880}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7b6428c3-ddc3-50c7-8b44-d4c45bc81ecd" :question/math-academy-id "q-3720" :question/problem "![](images/6a/6a225129d0879af950e935d794c09f3b479434154757a643c29c44a9d9e981e2.png)\n\nWhat is the length of $\\overset{―}{DE}?$" :question/worked-solution "From the figure, we note that the points $D$ and $E$ have coordinates ${{(-4,0)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{1}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{1})}$ and ${{(0,3)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{2}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{2})},$  respectively.\n\nTo find the length of $\\overset{―}{DE},$ we use the distance formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}DE & =\\sqrt{({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})^{2}+({y}_{2}-{y}_{1})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(0-(-4))^{2}+(3-0)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(4)^{2}+(3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
